 "title": "Register of Deeds | deuelcountysd",
 "text": "-->\nRegister of Deeds | deuelcountysd\ntop of page\nSkip to Main Content\nWelcome to Deuel County, South Dakota\nHOME\nDeuel County Commissioners\n2026 Commissioner Meetings\nArchived Commissioner Meeting Minutes\nList of County Offices\nAuditor\nClerk of Courts\nCommunity Health Nurse\nDirector of Equalization\nEmergency Management\n4-H Youth Program\nHighway Dept.\nICAP\nPlanning and Zoning\n2026 Zoning Meetings\nArchived Zoning Board Minutes\nRegister of Deeds\nSheriff's Office\nState's Attorney\nTreasurer\nVeterans Service Officer\nWeed Supervisor\nContact/More info\nCounty Job Opening\nCourthouse History\nTown & Township Contact Information\nMore\nUse tab to navigate through the menu items.\nRegister of Deeds\nThe Register of Deeds is the \"Library\" for the county. Our office records Deuel County real estate documents such as Deeds, Mortgages, Easements, Satisfactions, Plats, and other documents. Our office maintains full and true computerized and scanned records of all the documents. Many of these files can be obtained by calling, emailing, or visiting the county Register of Deeds office. For recording fees for South Dakota, please see the \"Fee Sheet to Record Documents in Reg. Deeds office\" link at the bottom of this page. Note: The Register of Deeds and staff CANNOT help you complete documents or forms. We are also unable to provide legal advice of any type. If you have questions about completing forms or how to transfer property, please consult with an attorney.\n​\nOther Documents Recorded:\nOur office also files/records documents such as:\nBurial Records\nCemetery Records\nMechanics Liens\nState, Federal, and County Liens\nMilitary Records\nUCC Documents\nAnd other miscellaneous documents\n​\nBirth, Death, and Marriage Certificates\nThe County Register of Deeds office can issue Certified copies of Birth, Death, and Marriage Certificates for a cost of $15.00 per copy. If you are unable to make it into our office you can mail us a completed form with correct fees using the application below or you can apply for a Certified copy online at www.vitalchek.com\nOur office also issues Marriage Licenses to anyone who plans to get married in South Dakota for a cost of $40.00. Marriage licenses can be obtained 90 days prior to the marriage. Both spouses need to be present and have a photo ID to apply. Individuals under the age of 18 will need a parent or guardian to sign the application. For more information about marriage requirements in South Dakota, please visit this website https://doh.sd.gov/records/marriage-requirements.aspx\n​\n​\nCasey Severson\nRegister of Deeds\nRenae Engelkes\nDeputy Register of Deeds\nPO Box 307\n408 4th St. West\nClear Lake, SD 57226\nPhone 605-874-2268\nFax 605-874-1306\n​\nHours\nMonday-Friday: 8:00 a.m.-5:00 p.m.\nClosed all state & federal holidays\n​\nOffice located on the second floor of the Courthouse.\n​\nrod@deuel.sdcounty.gov\nApplication and Forms\n*Marriage license application\n​\n*Vital Records Request Form\n​\n*Click here for a List of Fees to Record Documents\n​\n​\nHelpful Links\n*Link to Marriage License Requirements\n​\n*Certified copies information\n​\n*Apply for Marriage, Death, and Birth Certificate online\n​\n*Certificate of Real Estate Value\n​\n*Items Needed to Replace ID\n​\n​\n​\nClick here to\ngo HOME .\nCourthouse hours\n8:00 a.m. -5:00 p.m.\nClosed weekends and\nall state and federal holidays\n​\nCourthouse address\n408 4th Street West\nClear Lake, SD 57226\n© 2018 by Deuel County Proudly created with Wix.com\nPlease contact the specific office with your questions or concerns by clicking on the CONTACT US link below.\n​\nCONTACT US\nbottom of page",
